      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing the AI**\n\nI've decided to build a Python script, `detect_image_labels.py`, and have chosen Google Cloud Vision AI as the external provider for image label detection. The code will need a specific method to identify and interface with this provider. I'm now thinking about how to structure this identification.\n\n\n**Defining the Structure**\n\nNow, I'm fleshing out the structure of `detect_image_labels.py`. The plan is to directly integrate Google Cloud Vision AI using its specific libraries and client. I'll need to focus on how to use `google.cloud.vision_v1` and the `ImageAnnotatorClient` for object detection within the script.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861575728,
          "start": 1789861574139
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc1035fb0013p2FiH00o4X4xH",
